---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { emails, site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About — Ivan Minier"
  description="Ivan Minier is the founder of Tideframe Labs and a Business Administration student at the University of Vermont. He builds products and systems."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>I like systems that finally make sense.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I am Ivan Minier. I live in Vermont, study Business Administration at the University of Vermont,
        and founded Tideframe Labs. I design and build software, and sometimes I work on ideas that are not software at all.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p>
        The through-line is fairly ordinary. I keep running into systems that are useful in theory and exhausting in practice:
        a television catalog that looks like a spreadsheet, rental photos with no structure, a Mac that stays in one arrangement
        all day, campus housing that is hard to talk about clearly, laundry rooms you cannot see until you walk there.
      </p>
      <p>
        I try to understand those systems well enough to reorganize them. The finished thing should feel calm. Not empty. Just obvious.
      </p>

      <h2>What I care about</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="card"><strong>Products that explain themselves</strong><p>If a person has to decode the interface, the product is still part of the mess.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><strong>Calm power</strong><p>Software can be capable without being noisy. Native platforms help with that.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><strong>Private by default</strong><p>Rental records, playlists, and workspace profiles do not need to live on somebody else’s server.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><strong>Fragmented information, made usable</strong><p>The work is often just putting the right things next to each other.</p></article>
      </div>

      <h2>A short timeline</h2>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article><strong>Vermont</strong><p>Home base. Most of the work is designed and built here.</p></article>
        <article><strong>UVM</strong><p>Business Administration at the University of Vermont. Independent campus work includes LaundryLink and Trinity Redistricting.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Tideframe</strong><p>I founded Tideframe Labs as an independent software studio. Lineup, Tideframe Rental Record, and Modeboard live there.</p></article>
      </div>

      <h2>How to reach me</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={emails.primary.href}>{emails.primary.address}</a>.
        School mail is <a href={emails.school.href}>{emails.school.address}</a>.
        Personal mail is <a href={emails.personal.href}>{emails.personal.address}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
